WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.500
If there were a single mastermind 
behind everything

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.940
and killing them would solve everything,

00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:10.570
I'd go kill 'em right now.

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:15.950
We were powerless.

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:20.450
We had <i>two</i> mages and even an Arbiter,

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:22.820
and yet we still couldn't save him.

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:25.760
I should have accompanied you...

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:29.960
We won't get to work together forever.

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:36.240
If Hort and I take your magic provision 
for granted, we'll be useless.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:37.720
<b><i>Here lies Kady</i></b>

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:39.510
Ain't that right, Hort?

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:46.100
You shouldn't feel bad about that, Sayb.

00:00:55.490 --> 00:00:57.130
A dragon.

00:00:57.130 --> 00:00:58.470
It's the Dragon Conqueror King!

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:10.090
Dragon Conqueror King.

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:12.510
Ah, you three.

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:15.590
You have orders to return to Wenias.

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:17.510
Before long, this village

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:19.390
will be a battlefield.

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:54.190
What do you mean by "orders to return?"

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:54.190
Episode 11    Determination to Kill

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:55.940
What about what <i>we</i> want?

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:58.440
And what's this about a battlefield?

00:02:58.440 --> 00:03:00.120
It is as you were told.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:03.820
We cannot let students risk 
their lives on the battlefield.

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:07.480
Don't choose now to start 
acting like a normal teacher!

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:10.630
If there's gonna be a battle here, 
then you need all the help you can get!

00:03:10.630 --> 00:03:11.750
That's right!

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:13.630
You have been given instructions.

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:15.500
Follow them, or you'll be expelled.

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:18.160
Then I'll drop out.

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:19.300
Sayb?!

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:22.720
But if I prove useful in battle,

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:25.720
then please readmit me 
in recognition of my achievements.

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:27.670
Don't be ridiculous.

00:03:27.670 --> 00:03:29.180
That's quite a farce.

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:32.690
This war itself is a farce to begin with.

00:03:33.140 --> 00:03:38.400
Professor Los said that when mages 
are punched, they can't punch back.

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:43.490
In that case, this war is a 
thoroughly defensive battle.

00:03:43.490 --> 00:03:44.450
And?

00:03:45.020 --> 00:03:48.740
Professor Los said witches 
lay traps when they fight.

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:51.780
In which case, we just need 
to lay traps that won't kill people.

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:55.460
If we lay 100 traps that each 
incapacitate 10 people,

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:57.590
we can bring a force of 1,000 to zero.

00:03:57.590 --> 00:04:00.040
How will you make those traps?

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:03.300
To disable someone is far more 
difficult than to kill them.

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:05.510
With magic potions.

00:04:06.250 --> 00:04:07.790
You made one?

00:04:07.790 --> 00:04:10.020
A potion that supplies magic?

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:12.400
It's still unfinished,

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:15.940
but I can perfect it with Hort and Kudo.

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:19.610
And so, if we consult the Tyrant,

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:23.010
we can reduce the casualties due to magic.

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:28.770
If you managed that, I'd have to 
graduate you, not expel you.

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:34.690
A graduation exam is a fine idea!

00:04:34.690 --> 00:04:38.590
I am ever fond of innovative endeavors!

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:42.340
Dawn Witch, this is an Academy matter.

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:46.040
If thou sendest the students back,
 I too shall leave!

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:51.330
To me, this village's disappearance would 
hurt no more than the bite of a stray dog.

00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:53.190
That sounds pretty painful.

00:04:54.310 --> 00:04:55.890
Thou art right!

00:04:55.890 --> 00:04:58.770
I have taken a liking to this village!

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:01.920
Let me protect it! Let me fight!

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:06.130
Please! Please!

00:05:03.890 --> 00:05:06.610
All right, Dawn Witch. Don't throw a fit.

00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:10.050
I'll see what the 
Mooncaller Witch has to say.

00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:12.950
Hooray!

00:05:12.950 --> 00:05:14.960
Ah, my heart is dancing!

00:05:15.260 --> 00:05:19.080
I shall thrust those bloodthirsty 
fighters into a farce

00:05:19.610 --> 00:05:26.100
and, in front of everyone, make them 
a century-long subject of mockery!

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:35.180
Great. That sounds fantastic!

00:05:36.520 --> 00:05:39.060
Come. We have a grand performance to put on.

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:42.110
This doesn't really change anything.

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:46.820
You were planning from the beginning 
to conduct the fight so no one died.

00:05:46.820 --> 00:05:49.330
So? What flavor should it have?

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:52.460
Think about it from 
the audience's perspective.

00:05:52.460 --> 00:05:54.450
Instead of just silently ignoring them,

00:05:54.450 --> 00:05:58.760
it's more entertaining to tease 
the advance army and drive them away.

00:05:58.760 --> 00:06:01.090
Then it should really pop.

00:06:01.090 --> 00:06:02.720
I'll leave the casting to you.

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:05.500
I need to arrange an audience for the show.

00:06:10.840 --> 00:06:12.960
It's an odd feeling, isn't it?

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:18.940
To think former Arbiters would 
engage Church believers in battle.

00:06:19.780 --> 00:06:23.400
It's not like I was ever a believer.

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:25.530
I was just on death row.

00:06:26.490 --> 00:06:28.900
I hear you protected the children.

00:06:30.370 --> 00:06:33.740
Loux Krystas gave me a report.

00:06:34.580 --> 00:06:37.240
She said you're more 
compassionate than she thought.

00:06:39.480 --> 00:06:42.500
I just protected my owner, like a tool.

00:06:42.860 --> 00:06:46.460
I see. You claim not to 
follow your own will.

00:06:47.100 --> 00:06:51.000
And if the previous owner 
wishes to use the tool?

00:06:52.290 --> 00:06:55.430
The current owner will probably break it.

00:06:56.140 --> 00:06:58.590
I am concerned

00:06:58.590 --> 00:07:03.560
that the tool might suddenly break 
and injure the owner.

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:08.320
Well, the owner decides how much 
faith to place in their tools.

00:07:09.010 --> 00:07:11.200
And how does the owner do that?

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:13.960
The only way is to try the tool out, right?

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:15.640
In a safe environment?

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:18.200
That's what I would do.

00:07:18.850 --> 00:07:19.940
Where are you going?

00:07:19.940 --> 00:07:21.810
The teacher called for me.

00:07:21.810 --> 00:07:25.350
I see. It appears you've 
grown quite close with her.

00:07:25.350 --> 00:07:28.300
Giving a compliment wouldn't kill you.

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:32.140
Indeed, it is a joyous thing.

00:07:32.140 --> 00:07:33.620
May the divine protect you.

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:39.600
Amazing!

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:41.640
This really does replenish magic!

00:07:41.640 --> 00:07:43.120
This is amazing, Sayb!

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:44.770
So this is what you were making.

00:07:46.700 --> 00:07:49.280
You weren't just staying away from us.

00:07:49.540 --> 00:07:50.290
What?

00:07:50.290 --> 00:07:53.280
Uh, how did you make it?

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:58.560
Well, in Professor Zero's library, 
there was a book my father wrote.

00:07:58.560 --> 00:07:59.660
I used that.

00:07:59.660 --> 00:08:00.780
What?!

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:03.670
Y-Y-Yer pops was a sorcerer?!

00:08:04.420 --> 00:08:06.960
I'll tell you two this 
because I want you to know.

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:09.090
My father

00:08:09.810 --> 00:08:11.170
is Thirteen.

00:08:12.330 --> 00:08:17.800
Thirteen? He's... the bad guy 
who caused the war, right?

00:08:17.800 --> 00:08:18.870
Yeah.

00:08:20.210 --> 00:08:24.310
What the hell? It's like you're 
a chosen one or something!

00:08:24.310 --> 00:08:26.810
Of course you'd get special treatment!

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:29.440
You all-talent, no-hard-work jerk!

00:08:30.090 --> 00:08:31.210
Hey!

00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:33.740
I'm working hard now, too.

00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:35.210
Fairly hard.

00:08:35.210 --> 00:08:36.600
No...

00:08:36.600 --> 00:08:38.850
Maybe more like finally working hard?

00:08:40.480 --> 00:08:43.080
Yeah, I'm finally working hard.

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:50.500
Mr. Tyrant, thank you for saving us!

00:08:52.820 --> 00:08:54.740
Okay, eat up! Enjoy them!

00:08:55.130 --> 00:08:57.330
You don't look happy.

00:08:57.330 --> 00:09:00.600
Goodness. Maybe it was a little 
early for something like this.

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:04.440
It seems as though Mr. Tyrant 
is so happy that he's stunned.

00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:08.080
Go ahead, children. 
You can eat the treats now.

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:09.480
Yes, Ms. Hearthful!

00:09:10.500 --> 00:09:11.820
It looks so good!

00:09:12.500 --> 00:09:16.990
We all discussed how to thank you.

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:18.620
Oh, you did...

00:09:19.170 --> 00:09:24.620
I told them that Kady was receiving 
treatment in a bigger town.

00:09:24.620 --> 00:09:26.290
Oh, you did...

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:30.540
Are you going to try 
the treats the kids made?

00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:32.220
I don't—

00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:43.750
Your mind seems elsewhere.

00:09:44.610 --> 00:09:46.860
Would you like to talk to me about it?

00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:48.470
You can't help.

00:09:48.470 --> 00:09:50.540
Don't say that. Try me.

00:09:50.540 --> 00:09:52.230
You'll regret it.

00:09:52.880 --> 00:09:58.860
I prefer to take action and regret it,
rather than do nothing and regret it.

00:09:59.970 --> 00:10:05.290
What will make you and 
the kids suffer, cry, and scream?

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:07.530
It's constantly on my mind.

00:10:08.990 --> 00:10:11.460
Will you tell me, Teach?

00:10:12.120 --> 00:10:14.000
Are you...

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:16.470
saying you like me?

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:19.130
Wha—

00:10:19.130 --> 00:10:20.090
What?!

00:10:20.410 --> 00:10:23.210
It's okay. Don't be afraid.

00:10:23.210 --> 00:10:25.960
It's the same for everyone in the village.

00:10:25.960 --> 00:10:31.010
When they gain something precious, 
they imagine the moment it's destroyed,

00:10:31.490 --> 00:10:33.690
so they can find a way to protect it.

00:10:34.410 --> 00:10:36.170
To protect it?

00:10:36.170 --> 00:10:37.150
Thank you.

00:10:37.620 --> 00:10:41.030
You're trying to protect us, aren't you.

00:10:56.900 --> 00:10:58.310
You...

00:10:59.770 --> 00:11:03.800
...are just a tool, with no 
will of your own, right?

00:11:04.340 --> 00:11:09.100
You know, I'm not a big fan of Ms. Hearthful.

00:11:09.540 --> 00:11:12.760
I don't know what the Mask said to you,

00:11:12.760 --> 00:11:14.620
but I'll cut to the chase.

00:11:20.050 --> 00:11:22.160
I could do it.

00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:27.330
What, so you're saying you could 
even kill the person you fell for

00:11:27.330 --> 00:11:29.160
if you were ordered to?

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:31.130
That's how I was trained.

00:11:31.130 --> 00:11:33.860
Your tortured face suggests otherwise.

00:11:33.860 --> 00:11:36.630
Test me, then, if you have doubts.

00:11:37.620 --> 00:11:40.340
I just figured I'd torment you a little.

00:11:43.830 --> 00:11:47.270
Sayb is relying on your traps,

00:11:47.270 --> 00:11:49.830
to use in combination with his potions.

00:11:49.830 --> 00:11:51.570
But you see,

00:11:51.570 --> 00:11:55.000
that means your traps are 
a cornerstone of the plan, doesn't it?

00:11:55.000 --> 00:11:57.260
Frankly, I really don't like that,

00:11:57.770 --> 00:12:00.610
but I couldn't oppose it.

00:12:01.260 --> 00:12:06.700
Even human scum like you can protect people 
when their lives are suddenly in danger.

00:12:07.450 --> 00:12:11.080
You see, that really mixed things up for me.

00:12:11.650 --> 00:12:14.250
If you have feelings like a person,

00:12:14.250 --> 00:12:17.090
then more and more people 
will become important to you.

00:12:17.370 --> 00:12:22.800
If so, you'll suffer your whole life 
under the weight of everything you took.

00:12:24.060 --> 00:12:26.490
That'll be so very sad for you!

00:12:29.280 --> 00:12:33.470
If living will make you suffer, 
then keeping you alive is worth it.

00:12:33.470 --> 00:12:35.840
And so, I won't kill you.

00:12:35.840 --> 00:12:38.080
I'll even watch your back.

00:12:39.970 --> 00:12:40.780
Bye.

00:13:00.810 --> 00:13:04.280
So? Didst thou give her 
the idea for all that?

00:13:04.280 --> 00:13:07.850
I was certain that you had 
given her the idea.

00:13:07.850 --> 00:13:12.640
Do proper maintenance, 
entertain good doubts, then trust.

00:13:13.170 --> 00:13:16.650
No wonder Sayb and Kudo 
can be so carefree right now.

00:13:16.650 --> 00:13:19.690
Indeed. They are very observant.

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:21.980
Just like thee, eh?

00:13:21.980 --> 00:13:24.530
They'd be upset if you told them that.

00:13:25.080 --> 00:13:27.120
Oh? I would take it as a compliment.

00:13:32.010 --> 00:13:35.070
I guess he really is 
the right man for the job.

00:13:35.070 --> 00:13:37.670
It makes you want to call him "boss."

00:13:37.670 --> 00:13:40.730
Hey, boss, I have a question 
about this part of the blueprint.

00:13:40.730 --> 00:13:43.010
Do that to the west.

00:13:43.010 --> 00:13:44.660
They're already calling him that.

00:13:45.250 --> 00:13:46.380
So,

00:13:46.380 --> 00:13:50.080
why don't we target the Flagis spell 
at only their equipment?

00:13:50.080 --> 00:13:51.890
It's threatening enough.

00:13:51.890 --> 00:13:55.390
The most effective thing is to heavily 
injure them and then heal them.

00:13:55.390 --> 00:13:58.690
But won't that turn into 
a massacre if it goes wrong?

00:13:58.690 --> 00:14:01.270
Hmm. How about...

00:14:01.270 --> 00:14:03.300
Hold on, students.

00:14:03.300 --> 00:14:07.110
If we add another method 
of combined magic...

00:14:07.110 --> 00:14:09.510
They're really into this.

00:14:09.510 --> 00:14:11.970
What? Art thou not?

00:14:11.970 --> 00:14:15.140
We can only hope our opponents are weak.

00:14:15.140 --> 00:14:19.580
If the odds turn against us, 
we won't have the luxury of not killing.

00:14:19.580 --> 00:14:22.160
They are exceedingly weak.

00:14:22.540 --> 00:14:26.760
Farmers, poor people, the down 
and out. About 10,000 in total.

00:14:26.760 --> 00:14:27.940
Ten thousand?!

00:14:27.940 --> 00:14:29.920
'Tis quite the number.

00:14:29.920 --> 00:14:33.130
Killing people like that 
would make us the bad guys.

00:14:33.130 --> 00:14:35.330
That is no doubt their aim.

00:14:35.330 --> 00:14:36.780
There you are!

00:14:37.680 --> 00:14:40.690
There's food prep to do!

00:14:40.690 --> 00:14:43.460
Right, of course. I'm coming.

00:14:43.460 --> 00:14:47.020
Lilly, tonight the Dragon Conqueror King 
is going to take the villagers

00:14:47.020 --> 00:14:49.690
and fly them to Loutra Cathedral.

00:14:49.690 --> 00:14:52.090
You leave the village with them.

00:14:53.350 --> 00:14:54.150
Uh-Uh!

00:14:54.150 --> 00:14:54.870
Excuse me?

00:14:54.870 --> 00:14:57.490
I'm really strong.

00:14:57.490 --> 00:15:00.500
I'm gonna fight with you and protect you!

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:02.140
Aren't I?

00:15:02.140 --> 00:15:05.770
You certainly are. 
You're stronger than me, after all.

00:15:05.770 --> 00:15:07.330
What's this?

00:15:07.330 --> 00:15:12.440
This cute little mouse girl is that strong?

00:15:12.440 --> 00:15:14.350
Thou art like me!

00:15:16.080 --> 00:15:18.910
Even softer than I imagined!

00:15:18.910 --> 00:15:20.040
Priest, you scoundrel.

00:15:20.040 --> 00:15:24.490
Thou art fully appreciating such 
a wonderful creature every day?

00:15:24.490 --> 00:15:25.500
How darest thou?

00:15:25.500 --> 00:15:26.860
I am not.

00:15:26.860 --> 00:15:28.360
You're making her uncomfortable.

00:15:28.360 --> 00:15:29.770
I'm separating you.

00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:34.320
Oh, you aren't? I always assumed you—

00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:38.080
You big dummy!

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:39.230
I hate you!

00:15:40.080 --> 00:15:41.880
Wait!

00:15:42.460 --> 00:15:43.800
Lilly, come back!

00:15:43.800 --> 00:15:44.890
'Tis futile.

00:15:44.890 --> 00:15:46.960
This farce will go down in history.

00:15:47.790 --> 00:15:51.640
'Twould be sad to leave someone 
who wishes to participate out.

00:15:51.640 --> 00:15:55.100
She has no such wish.

00:15:55.100 --> 00:15:56.850
What does she have, then?

00:15:57.530 --> 00:15:59.730
Wouldn't it be love for me?

00:16:00.900 --> 00:16:02.130
What is wrong?

00:16:02.130 --> 00:16:04.730
I was stunned by that extreme confidence!

00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:07.360
But on to a more important matter.

00:16:08.210 --> 00:16:12.490
This is the Remnant of Disaster 
that ate through Kady's stomach.

00:16:12.490 --> 00:16:14.520
This is just a model.

00:16:14.990 --> 00:16:17.120
If I had not exterminated it,

00:16:17.120 --> 00:16:22.330
it would have spread out infinitely 
from the village and devoured the populace.

00:16:22.330 --> 00:16:25.650
Which raises a question.

00:16:25.650 --> 00:16:27.070
A question?

00:16:27.070 --> 00:16:32.530
Did the Church extremists intend to take 
themselves out along with the witches?

00:16:32.970 --> 00:16:38.350
No one is foolish enough to spread a plague 
without first preparing a cure.

00:16:38.630 --> 00:16:41.090
And supposing that the upper 
echelons of the Church,

00:16:41.090 --> 00:16:45.600
perhaps not even the bishops, 
know how to deal with this?

00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:50.230
Then whoever knows how to stop it 
is the one who spread it.

00:16:52.370 --> 00:16:55.670
The dragon is flying 
to Loutra Cathedral tonight, yes?

00:16:55.670 --> 00:16:58.590
Might there be a seat reserved for me?

00:16:59.820 --> 00:17:01.960
Don't dispatch the troops?!

00:17:01.960 --> 00:17:06.500
Are you telling the Church & Mage Knights 
to ignore this oppression of witches?

00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:08.060
Calm down.

00:17:08.060 --> 00:17:11.470
They won't be fighting, 
but we will send troops.

00:17:11.470 --> 00:17:13.170
What do you mean?

00:17:13.170 --> 00:17:18.940
We'll be taking care of those 
who flee the witch village.

00:17:20.390 --> 00:17:26.230
We'll treat their injuries, feed them, 
and let them listen to the band.

00:17:26.620 --> 00:17:32.480
They're idiots whipped up by simplistic 
speeches claiming "witches are all bad."

00:17:32.840 --> 00:17:35.730
If we treat them well, 
they'll be on our side.

00:17:35.730 --> 00:17:37.280
But then...

00:17:37.280 --> 00:17:41.170
This will wind up requiring even more 
soldiers than if we annihilated them.

00:17:41.170 --> 00:17:45.280
Yes. Which is why I ask you, Knight Captain.

00:17:46.120 --> 00:17:48.170
How many can you get?

00:17:48.460 --> 00:17:54.050
Ria, a request from the Church & Mage 
Knights to dispatch the Magic Medic Unit.

00:17:54.050 --> 00:17:58.050
Church extremists are marching 
against Zero and Mercenary's village

00:17:58.050 --> 00:18:00.930
with a force 10,000 strong.

00:18:00.930 --> 00:18:02.520
How awful.

00:18:02.520 --> 00:18:04.900
Those 10,000 people are going to die.

00:18:05.430 --> 00:18:07.890
Yeah, they don't do well with holding back.

00:18:08.280 --> 00:18:12.920
Will things be okay if I leave a single 
medic here as a proxy in my absence?

00:18:12.920 --> 00:18:15.400
We have so many more magic medics now,

00:18:15.780 --> 00:18:18.910
you could even abdicate your 
position as Saint if you'd like.

00:18:20.780 --> 00:18:22.280
Hey! Don't rib me like that!

00:18:23.530 --> 00:18:26.410
From Faeria, the Ruler 
of the Holy City Acdios.

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:31.060
An emergency message to Torres, 
Head of State of the Creon Republic.

00:18:33.130 --> 00:18:34.420
Fantastic!

00:18:34.420 --> 00:18:36.260
A fantastic venture!

00:18:36.730 --> 00:18:39.230
I have always thought 
that war ought to be conducted

00:18:39.230 --> 00:18:41.190
through a game played on a board.

00:18:41.190 --> 00:18:47.330
But to conduct that game
 on the battlefield...!

00:18:45.740 --> 00:18:48.480
Ow. Not so hard, Torres.

00:18:48.480 --> 00:18:54.190
Now, about that Remnant of Disaster 
from your report the other day.

00:18:54.190 --> 00:18:56.610
We have determined where it came from.

00:18:56.610 --> 00:18:57.710
Really?

00:18:57.710 --> 00:18:58.860
Indeed!

00:19:00.110 --> 00:19:03.910
It started with a noble 
who loved stories of adventure.

00:19:03.910 --> 00:19:10.300
He hired troops, marched to the north, 
and then lost half his troops in a day.

00:19:10.300 --> 00:19:15.670
In the bodies they managed to bring back, 
Remnant of Disaster seeds were found.

00:19:16.010 --> 00:19:18.850
So, the noble went crying to the Church,

00:19:18.850 --> 00:19:21.300
which took them and secretly 
passed them to the extremists.

00:19:21.920 --> 00:19:23.430
Which means...

00:19:23.430 --> 00:19:27.480
a great number of Remnants 
of Disaster could still appear.

00:19:28.660 --> 00:19:29.720
Take this.

00:19:31.940 --> 00:19:36.940
The noble brought back roughly 
500 bodies from the north.

00:19:36.940 --> 00:19:41.510
Supposing they all contained 
Remnants of Disaster,

00:19:42.110 --> 00:19:46.120
when and where would they use them?

00:19:46.120 --> 00:19:48.760
We may have been underestimating them.

00:19:48.760 --> 00:19:50.870
Albus! I didn't know you were here.

00:19:52.170 --> 00:19:55.000
Torres, I brought an emergency 
message from Ria.

00:19:55.410 --> 00:19:56.500
Here it is.

00:19:56.500 --> 00:19:58.900
Cal! Perfect timing!

00:19:58.900 --> 00:20:02.630
Could you fly north right now 
and call back the Mage Commander?

00:20:02.630 --> 00:20:04.010
The north?!

00:20:04.010 --> 00:20:07.430
Ask the Dragon Conqueror King! 
I still wanna live!

00:20:07.430 --> 00:20:09.370
Don't worry! You'll be fine.

00:20:09.370 --> 00:20:13.000
The Commander will make sure to protect you.

00:20:13.640 --> 00:20:15.810
Go as fast as possible! Right now!

00:20:15.810 --> 00:20:17.940
How merciless...

00:20:17.940 --> 00:20:21.690
Well, Torres, you gather the audience.

00:20:21.690 --> 00:20:25.240
I need to return to 
the academy and inform Zero.

00:20:26.500 --> 00:20:27.900
Sayb.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:32.210
Uls. Laios.

00:20:32.710 --> 00:20:37.960
I'm leaving the village tomorrow, 
even though I actually wanna stay and fight.

00:20:37.960 --> 00:20:40.310
But since I'm still a kid...

00:20:40.860 --> 00:20:42.090
Of course.

00:20:42.600 --> 00:20:46.180
But I'll grow up and come 
back as fast as I can!

00:20:47.320 --> 00:20:51.490
I'll be waiting, for when 
you come back as an adult.

00:20:51.490 --> 00:20:55.220
Make sure you hold out until I come back.

00:20:56.260 --> 00:21:00.180
The outcome of war is largely 
determined by preparation.

00:21:00.180 --> 00:21:05.150
How many troops you've mustered. 
How strong a fortress you've built.

00:21:05.500 --> 00:21:08.870
The other side has made 
preparations to kill us.

00:21:07.350 --> 00:21:08.870
Ready!

00:21:09.530 --> 00:21:14.040
But we've been preparing to not kill them.

00:21:14.460 --> 00:21:17.920
If we fail, we'll end up killing people.

00:21:20.690 --> 00:21:23.420
Professor Zero, if I may.

00:21:27.430 --> 00:21:29.530
Young man, what are you doing?

00:21:30.090 --> 00:21:32.090
This is the most rational move.

00:21:32.090 --> 00:21:33.680
You have an obligation

00:21:33.680 --> 00:21:38.230
to do everything in your power to protect 
our futures and the future of mages.

00:21:38.930 --> 00:21:42.780
As such, even if my 
individual future is ruined...

00:21:42.780 --> 00:21:44.050
Sayb!

00:21:50.960 --> 00:21:55.990
How much magical energy to give me 
is your decision, young man.

00:21:56.410 --> 00:21:58.580
I shall accept it.

00:21:59.690 --> 00:22:01.190
I'm going full throttle.

00:22:14.890 --> 00:22:16.850
Ludicrous! Just how far does it go?

00:22:25.260 --> 00:22:27.110
P-Professor Zero?

00:22:27.970 --> 00:22:30.110
Do you... feel okay?

00:22:30.460 --> 00:22:32.650
I feel a little lighter.

00:22:33.360 --> 00:22:36.620
So this is what it feels like 
to have less magic.

00:22:37.500 --> 00:22:39.060
I was underestimating you...

00:22:41.180 --> 00:22:44.880
You will one day make a name 
for yourself as a sorcerer.

00:22:45.340 --> 00:22:47.680
Just as I am known as the Mud-Black Witch,

00:22:47.680 --> 00:22:49.880
and Albus is known as the Mooncaller...

00:22:50.690 --> 00:22:52.370
The Abyss Sorcerer.

00:22:52.840 --> 00:22:57.640
When someone eventually 
inquires for your name,

00:22:57.640 --> 00:22:59.740
that is what I shall call you.

00:23:00.400 --> 00:23:02.570
Um... I...

00:23:03.900 --> 00:23:06.130
Loosen up! Stand tall and proud!

00:23:06.130 --> 00:23:08.150
You don't need to be anxious!

00:23:08.150 --> 00:23:12.000
It's for after you've accomplished 
something so great people ask who you are!

00:23:12.000 --> 00:23:13.010
That's right.

00:23:13.010 --> 00:23:15.700
And if you mess up in this war,

00:23:15.700 --> 00:23:17.940
then all three of you 
will be expelled together.

00:23:17.940 --> 00:23:19.710
What?!

00:23:27.840 --> 00:23:29.770
A demon-possessed, huh?

00:23:30.460 --> 00:23:33.470
Looks like they're not quite 
as ragtag as we expected.

00:23:37.740 --> 00:23:40.550
Witness, my friend.

00:23:41.990 --> 00:23:45.840
Thou, too, wilt surely 
appreciate this farce.

00:23:48.980 --> 00:23:50.420
My dear Ludens,

00:23:52.750 --> 00:23:54.400
say hello!

00:23:55.520 --> 00:24:00.000
What dost thou think is required 
to beat an enemy without killing them?

00:23:57.870 --> 00:24:10.010
<b>Next Episode
 "The Beginning of the Adventure"</b>

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:02.540
'Tis overwhelming superiority.

00:24:03.040 --> 00:24:05.790
Next episode: "The Beginning of the Adventure."

00:24:05.790 --> 00:24:06.880
Very well!

00:24:06.880 --> 00:24:09.650
You will bring those words 
to my lips, won't you?
